{
  "slug": "repo-intel",
  "name": "Repo Intel",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Unified static analysis for AI agents — git history, AST symbols, project metadata, doc-code sync, and (optionally) LLM-augmented file descriptors plus a 3-depth narrative summary, via a cached, incrementally-updatable Rust binary. Scan a repo once, cache the result, then query it repeatedly. The heavy lifting runs in [agent-analyzer](https://github.com/agent-sh/agent-analyzer) (Rust) — this plugin provides the JavaScript interface, the skill layer that other plugins consume, and the orchestration that spawns Haiku subagents to enrich the artifact with semantic signals. Other agentsys plugins (drift-detect, can-i-help, audit-project, onboard) consume the same artifact without re-scanning.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, **3 agents** and **1 command**.\n\n- **Skills** (1): `repo-intel` (Use when user asks to \\\"analyze git history\\\", \\\"show hotspots\\\", \\\"coldspots\\\", \\\"file coupling\\\", \\\"code ownership\\\", \\\"bus factor\\\", \\\"bugspots\\\",…)\n- **Agents** (3): `map-validator` (Validate repo-intel output for obvious errors and missing data), `repo-intel-summarizer` (Produce a 3-depth narrative description of a repository (1-line, 1-paragraph, 1-page) for AI agents and humans landing in…), `repo-intel-weighter` (Generate concrete one-sentence descriptors for source files so the repo-intel find scorer can match user concept queries (e.g)\n- **Commands** (1): `repo-intel` (Unified static analysis - git history, AST symbols, project metadata, doc-code sync, plus LLM-augmented file descriptors and a…)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install repo-intel@claude-community` from `agent-sh/repo-intel`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "skill": 1,
    "agent": 3,
    "command": 1
  },
